{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user issued a **Phase 3A batch translation** prompt for the `c2rust` branch of the picoquic project. The task: translate C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies under `rs/fq/src/tests/`. Five source batches were assigned:\n   - `flow_control_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/flow_control.rs`\n   - `getter_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/getter.rs`\n   - `hashtest` (4 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/hashtest.rs`\n   - `high_latency_test` (4 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/high_latency.rs`\n   - `intformattest` (3 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/intformattest.rs`\n\n   Requirements: faithful body translation (no `todo!()` placeholders), compile-not-pass gate, no `unsafe`, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/`, `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`, or `todo!()` stubs in `rs/fq/src/{internal,lib}.rs`. After each source, run `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py <src>`. At the end run `cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Rust translation of C picoquic QUIC library on the `c2rust` branch\n   - Crate at `rs/fq/`; `Instant = fugit::Instant<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` (microseconds); `Duration = fugit::Duration<u64, 1, 1_000_000>`\n   - `StreamDataCallback` trait replaces C `void(*fn_ptr)(...)` + `void* callback_ctx`\n   - `Rc<RefCell<T>>` used for shared mutable callback state (matches cnxstress.rs pattern)\n   - `CallbackEvent` enum replaces C `picoquic_call_back_event_t`\n   - `HashTable<K: Hash+Eq, V>` with `HashToken` replaces intrusive C `picohash_table`\n   - `Connection::next_wake_time` is a **public field** (`pub next_wake_time: Instant`), not a method\n   - `find_path_by_address` exists in `internal.rs` with signature `(Option<&SocketAddr>, Option<&SocketAddr>, &mut i32) -> i32`\n   - `PrepareToSend` callback event uses `todo!()` since `provide_stream_data_buffer` context not yet wired through Rust callback API (consistent with cnxstress.rs pattern)\n   - `tls_api_init_ctx_ex2` wraps `tls_api_init_ctx_ex` in util.rs\n   - `get_congestion_algorithm(\"name\")` replaces direct C algorithm pointer references\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/lib.rs`** — Added 11 stub methods:\n     - In `impl Quic`: `pub fn cwin_max(&self) -> u64` (after `set_cwin_max`); `pub fn earliest_cnx_to_wake(&mut self, _wake_time: Instant) -> Option<&mut Connection>` (after `next_wake_time`)\n     - In `impl Connection`: `pub fn set_cnx_spinbit_policy(&mut self, _policy: SpinbitVersion)`, `pub fn cnx_spinbit_policy(&self) -> SpinbitVersion` (after `padding_policy`); `pub fn has_misc_frames(&self) -> bool`, `pub fn misc_frames_is_singleton(&self) -> bool`, `pub fn delete_last_misc_frame(&mut self)`, `pub fn quic_time(&self) -> Instant` (before closing `}` of misc frame block); `pub fn set_stream_remote_error(&mut self, _stream_id: u64, _error_code: u64)` (after `remote_stream_error`); `pub fn preemptive_repeat_count(&self) -> u64` (after `set_preemptive_repeat`)\n     - Also removed the duplicate `find_path_by_address` that was accidentally added\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/internal.rs`** — Added 1 stub:\n     - `pub fn frames_varint_encode_length(_n64: u64) -> usize` (after `encode_varint_length`)\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`** — Added `tls_api_init_ctx_ex2`:\n     ```rust\n     pub fn tls_api_init_ctx_ex2(\n         simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n         proposed_version: u32,\n         _sni: Option<&str>,\n         _alpn: Option<&str>,\n         ticket_file: Option<&str>,\n         initial_cid: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n     ) -> Option<Box<TestTlsApiCtx>> {\n         tls_api_init_ctx_ex(simulated_time, proposed_version, ticket_file, initial_cid)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/intformattest.rs`** — Updated `sqrt_for_test()`:\n     - Added inline `fn sqrt_for_tests(y: u64) -> u64` helper (mirrors C `picoquic_sqrt_for_tests`)\n     - Replaced `todo!(\"sqrt_for_test_test (no Rust counterpart yet)\")` with full loop: `x_base doubling sequence, both i∈{0,1}, assert sqrt_for_tests(x_base*(x_base+i)) == x_base`\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/hashtest.rs`** — Complete rewrite:\n     - Added `fn hash_test_init(test: &mut [u8], k: &mut [u8; 16])` shared helper (deterministic data+key init)\n     - `picohash()`: uses `HashTable::<u64, ()>::new(32)`, inserts odds 1..9, collision inserts, lookup checks, delete checks\n     - `picohash_embedded()`: identical logic but uses `HashTable::with_seed(32, &hash_seed)`\n     - `picohash_bytes()`: calls `crate::hash::hash_bytes(&test[..len], &k)` and checks 12 known answers\n     - `siphash()`: refactored to use shared `hash_test_init()`, keeps same known-answer table\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/high_latency.rs`** — Complete rewrite:\n     - `HILAT_SCENARIO_100MB`: const array of 100 `TestApiStreamDesc` (stream ids 4,8,12,...400, each 1MB response)\n     - `fn high_latency_one(test_id, ccalgo, scenario, max_completion_time, latency, mbps_up, mbps_down, jitter, has_loss, do_preemptive, seed_bw)`:\n       - Builds `TransportParameters` with `enable_time_stamp = 3` for both client/server\n       - Builds `initial_cid` with encoded test params in bytes 2-7\n       - Calls `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex()`\n       - Sets congestion algorithm, link params, preemptive repeat\n       - Uses `server_addr.ip()` for `seed_bandwidth` (IpAddr from SocketAddr)\n       - Calls `tls_api_one_scenario_body()` then asserts `preemptive_repeat_count() > 0` if `do_preemptive`\n     - 4 tests: `high_latency_basic` (newreno, latency*7), `high_latency_bbr` (145s), `high_latency_cubic` (200s), `high_latency_probeRTT` (1Mbps, 839s)\n     - Uses `get_congestion_algorithm(\"reno\"/\"bbr\"/\"cubic\")` instead of algorithm pointers\n     - `let _ = test_ctx.qserver.set_qlog(\".\");` to suppress unused Result\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/flow_control.rs`** — Complete rewrite:\n     - `#[allow(dead_code)] struct FctestShared { transfer_size, microsecs_per_byte, credit_quantum, simulated_time, stream_id, bytes_sent, bytes_received, bytes_buffered, buffered_time, microsec_rounding_error, credits_pending, bytes_buffered_max, is_started, fin_sent, fin_received, is_closed, error_detected }`\n     - `struct FctestCallback(Rc<RefCell<FctestShared>>)`\n     - `impl StreamDataCallback for FctestCallback` — handles StreamData/Fin (client calls `fctest_receive_data`, server calls `mark_active_stream`), Close events set `is_closed`, PrepareToSend uses `todo!()`, AlmostReady/Ready calls `fctest_start_stream`\n     - `fn fctest_start_stream(ctx, cnx)`: calls `cnx.get_next_local_stream_id(false)`, `cnx.add_to_stream()`, `cnx.set_app_flow_control()`\n     - `fn fctest_receive_data(ctx, cnx, current_time, length)`: credit accounting, calls `cnx.open_flow_control()`\n     - `fn fctest_one(test_id, ccalgo, loss_mask_init, transfer_size, microsecs_per_byte, credit_quantum, initial_credit, _bytes_buffered_max_limit, completion_target)`: creates shared context, calls `tls_api_init_ctx_ex2()`, installs two `FctestCallback` (one each via `set_default_callback` and `set_callback`), runs connection loop, then sim loop updating `shared.simulated_time` each iteration\n     - `flow_control()` test: `get_congestion_algorithm(\"bbr\")`, params: transfer=1M, microsecs_per_byte=10, credit_quantum=0x4000, initial_credit=0x10000, completion_target=11M\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/getter.rs`** — Complete rewrite:\n     - Creates test context with `tls_api_init_ctx_ex2()`\n     - Tests `set_default_connection_id_length(255)` → `Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::CnxidCheck as u64))`\n     - Tests `set_default_connection_id_length(5)` → `Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::CannotChangeActiveContext as u64))`\n     - `default_connection_id_ttl()`, `default_tp()`, `cwin_max()`/`set_cwin_max(0)` → u64::MAX\n     - `find_path_by_address(None, Some(&peer), &mut partial: i32)` from internal.rs\n     - `set_local_addr()` first succeeds, second fails\n     - `queue_misc_frame(&mf, false, PacketContext::Initial)`, `purge_misc_frames_after_ready()`, `has_misc_frames()`, `delete_last_misc_frame()`, `misc_frames_is_singleton()`\n     - After handshake: `local_connection_id()`, `remote_connection_id()`, `initial_connection_id()`, `client_connection_id()`, `server_connection_id()`\n     - `set_padding_policy(256, 55)`, `padding_policy()` roundtrip\n     - `set_cnx_spinbit_policy(SpinbitVersion::Random)`, `cnx_spinbit_policy()` roundtrip\n     - `is_sslkeylog_enabled()`, `is_handshake_error()` checks\n     - `register_all_congestion_control_algorithms()`, `get_congestion_algorithm(name)` for 7 algorithms\n     - `set_default_congestion_algorithm_by_name(\"dcubic\")` with `let _ = ...`\n     - `enable_keep_alive(Duration::from_ticks(0))`, `enable_keep_alive(l_timer)`, `disable_keep_alive()`\n     - `set_stream_remote_error(0, app_error)`, `remote_stream_error(0)` roundtrip\n     - `adjust_max_connections(4)`, `current_number_connections() == 1`\n     - `default_crypto_epoch_length()`, `set_crypto_epoch_length(0)`, `crypto_epoch_length()`\n     - `local_cid_length()`, `is_local_cid(&fake)` false, `is_local_cid(&local)` true\n     - `set_max_simultaneous_logs(17)`, `max_simultaneous_logs() == 17`\n     - `set_max_half_open_retry_threshold(17)`, `max_half_open_retry_threshold() == 17`\n     - `register_net_icid()` second call should err\n     - `next_wake_time(simulated_time)` on Quic, `earliest_cnx_to_wake(half)` should be None\n     - `cnx.next_wake_time.ticks()` (field access, not method!), `wake_delay(test_time, i64::MAX)`, `wake_delay(test_time, delay/2)`\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n   - **Duplicate `find_path_by_address`**: Added one in lib.rs but internal.rs already has one with different signature `(Option<&SocketAddr>, Option<&Socke